  "_readme": "SOURCE OF TRUTH for the C64 game feasibility matrix. Edit this file, then run `node scripts/gen-capability-matrix.mjs` (or `yarn gen:matrix`) to regenerate docs/game-feasibility-matrix.html. Verdict keys: clean|caveated|blocked. Confidence keys: known|inferred|low. Diff: S|M|L|XL. Blocker codes must exist in legend.blockerCodes (a trailing qualifier in parentheses, e.g. SAMPLE(minor), is allowed). Summary counts and inversion counts are DERIVED by the generator — never stored here.",
  "meta": {
    "title": "Blend65 — C64 Game Feasibility Matrix",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-07-17",
    "refreshWith": "/update_capability"
  },
  "intro": {
    "purpose": [
      "A strict, capability-grounded assessment of whether 100 well-known Commodore 64 games could be built **faithfully** with the Blend65 toolchain — as it stands the day RD-18 closes (unoptimized codegen), and again after the Phase B optimizer lands. It doubles as a prioritization tool: every blocker is a code, so the inversion table at the bottom shows what shipping each capability *unlocks*.",
      "**No sugarcoating.** A game is only ✅ if it can be built as the original *played* — right engine, right controls, clean in-language audio, no missing essentials, and no dropping to hand-poked machine-code bytes. \"Close enough\" is ⚠️, not ✅."
    ]
  },
  "baseline": {
    "asOf": "2026-07-17",
    "intro": "The verdicts are only as current as this snapshot. When it changes, re-run `/update_capability`.",
    "rows": [
      {
        "capability": "Frozen v3 language (scalars, structs, arrays, enums, strings, functions, modules, full expressions, control flow, by-ref params, interrupts, `zeropage`, `&`-address-of, `embed()`, intrinsics)",
