  "inversion": {
    "intro": "Read this to decide what to build *after* RD-18. Counts are the number of the 100 titles a capability gates (it appears in the title's Blockers or Path to 100%).",
    "rows": [
      { "code": "OPT", "label": "Phase B optimizer", "impact": "**The single biggest unlock.** Moves the bulk of ❌→⚠️ (nearly every scroller/shmup/brawler) and a band of ⚠️→✅. Everything perf-bound depends on it. Already on the roadmap." },
      { "code": "DISK", "label": "disk multi-load / streaming", "impact": "**The biggest *hard-gap* unlock.** Frees all the RPGs (Ultima, Bard's Tale, Pool of Radiance), SCUMM adventures, Cinemaware, Epyx multi-event sports, and the streamed Last Ninjas. None reachable without it — no spec story exists today." },
      { "code": "FUT-011", "label": "external asm + fast math", "impact": "Unblocks real-time 3D (Elite, Mercenary), sprite-scaling racers (Out Run), and the cycle-exact scroll showcase (Mayhem in Monsterland) — the 50 fps / vector ceiling `OPT` alone can't reach." },
      { "code": "FLOAT", "label": "fixed-point math", "impact": "Fractional physics: golf (Leaderboard), marble/ball physics (Marble Madness, Spindizzy), racer road math. Feasible by hand today (that's why several are ⚠️, not ❌); a library would make them clean." },
      { "code": "FUT-003", "label": "indirect calls", "impact": "Needed for true VM/dispatch-table engines (SCUMM). Also the clean fix for invoking a ripped `.sid` player and for jump-table dispatch everywhere — a broad quality-of-life unlock beyond the raw count." },
      { "code": "SAMPLE", "label": "in-language sample player", "impact": "Digitized speech (Impossible Mission, Ghostbusters-class). Doable in-language with tight timing; not a language gap, an effort gap." }
    ],
    "bottomLine": "**Bottom line for sequencing:** `OPT` first (already planned, unlocks the most and the flashiest arcade action), then a **`DISK`/loader story** (unlocks the entire \"epic\" catalogue that `OPT` can never touch), then `FUT-011` + a fast fixed-point math library for the 3D/showcase tier."
  },
  "provenance": [
    "**The list is curated, not a sourced ranking.** These are 100 well-known, category-spanning C64 titles — not \"the top 100\" by any measured metric (sales, Zzap!64 score, Lemon64 votes). Swap freely with `/update_capability`.",
    "**Verdicts are anchored on *engine archetype*, which is the real feasibility driver**, then adjusted for a title's specifics. Where a specific game's internals are inferred rather than known, the **Conf** column says so (⚠️/🔴) — treat those rows as archetype estimates, not reverse-engineered fact.",
    "**Faithfulness bar is strict**: ✅ means the original *as played*. A reduced-scope demake that captures the feel but drops the smooth scroll, the multiplexed sprite count, the disk-streamed content, or the exact soundtrack is **⚠️**, not ✅ — even when it would be a perfectly good game.",
    "**\"Original soundtrack\" footnote applies to every row** (see the About audio note): in-language music is clean, but a byte-faithful reproduction of the ripped `.sid` tune needs `FUT-003`. Not repeated per row."
  ],
  "footer": "Maintained via `/update_capability`. When the capability baseline changes (a slice/RD closes, Phase B lands, a `DISK`/`FUT-003`/`FUT-011` capability ships), re-run it to re-score every row and refresh the summary + inversion counts."
}
